Modern first-letter tables (src/modern/data)
===========================================

The modern common and full tables are generated from pinyin.txt and
kMandarin_8105.txt in mozillazg/pinyin-data:
https://github.com/mozillazg/pinyin-data/tree/923b108dc5d45dee061324c011b478fb649f8b73
Source commit: 923b108dc5d45dee061324c011b478fb649f8b73

Pyfl removes tone marks, retains the first ASCII letter of each reading,
deduplicates alternatives, and uses kMandarin_8105 preferred readings where
available. The bundled phrase rules are maintained by Pyfl separately.

The direct pinyin-data project carries the MIT notice reproduced below.
Its Unicode-derived data remains subject to the Unicode notice also reproduced
below; it is not relabeled MIT. The pinned upstream README records its Unihan
fields, dictionary references, and manual-correction sources:
https://github.com/mozillazg/pinyin-data/blob/923b108dc5d45dee061324c011b478fb649f8b73/README.md

Original source notices and their verified hashes are retained in the repository
under experimental/initials/data/licenses, upstream, and source-lock.json.

